### Provider Connections API

@URL = http://localhost:8080
@AUTH_TOKEN = your-token
@connectionId = replace-with-connection-id
@provider = nosana

# NOTE: The user NEVER sends credential_secret_id.
# The provider defines its own fields (schema). Backend calls the provider to
# split the user input into `config` (stored raw) and `secret` (encrypted at rest),
# then creates the Secret row itself and links it to the connection.

### Get connection schema (form fields for a provider)
# Use this to render the connection form. Each field carries:
#   key, name, type, required, secret, default, placeholder, options
# type: text | password | number | boolean | select | file
GET {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/schema?provider={{provider}}
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}

### Verify provider credentials (dry-run, nothing saved)
# Drives the green check in the UI before the user clicks Connect.
# Accepts either JSON or multipart/form-data (when a file field is present).
POST {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "nosana",
  "api_key": "nos_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
  "base_url": "https://api.nosana.com"
}

### List Provider Connections
GET {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}

### Create Provider Connection
# Only provider + name + provider-defined fields. No credential_secret_id.
POST {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "nosana",
  "name": "nosana-prod",
  "api_key": "nos_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
  "base_url": "https://api.nosana.com"
}

### Create Provider Connection (with file upload, e.g. GCP service account)
# Use multipart/form-data when the schema has a `file` field.
# Backend reads the file bytes and passes them to the provider.
POST {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----ORCNBoundary

------ORCNBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="provider"

gcp
------ORCNBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

gcp-prod
------ORCNBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="service_account"; filename="service-account.json"
Content-Type: application/json

< ./service-account.json
------ORCNBoundary--

### Get Provider Connection
GET {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/{{connectionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}

### Re-verify a saved connection
POST {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/{{connectionId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}

### Update Provider Connection
PUT {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/{{connectionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "nosana-prod-updated",
  "api_key": "nos_newkey"
}

### Delete Provider Connection
DELETE {{URL}}/api/v1/provider-connections/{{connectionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{AUTH_TOKEN}}
